{"type":"assistant","uuid":"1b2448f7-8bee-4539-8c3c-3b85911c0bce","session_id":"ac3c3c7e-3944-4bdf-8f73-f3460c81d597","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"1b2448f7-8bee-4539-8c3c-3b85911c0bce","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. The bug is in `DocumentEditFragment.onResume()`. Let me look at the key evidence:\n\n1. `HighlightingEditor` extends `AppCompatEditText`, which extends `EditText` - so it has `getSelectionStart()` and `setSelection()` methods.\n\n2. In `DocumentEditFragment.loadDocumentIntoUi()` (line 135-138), the cursor position is properly preserved:\n```java\nint editorpos = _hlEditor.getSelectionStart();\n_hlEditor.setText(_document.getContent());\neditorpos = editorpos > _hlEditor.length() ? _hlEditor.length() - 1 : editorpos;\n\n\n```\n\nSetting cursor position:\n```java\n_hlEditor.setSelection(editorpos < 0 ? 0 : editorpos);\n```\n\n3. But in `DocumentEditFragment.onResume()` (line 107-110):\n```java\n@Override\npublic void onResume() {\n    super.onResume();\n    checkReloadDisk();\n    _hlEditor.setText(_document.getContent());  // <-- BUG: resets cursor to 0\n}\n```\n\nThe fix: In `onResume()`, preserve the cursor position before calling `setText()`, just like `loadDocumentIntoUi()` does. I need to capture the current selection position before replacing the text, then restore it afterward using the same clamping logic to ensure it stays within bounds.\n\n```\n\njava\n@Override\npublic void onResume() {\n    super.onResume();\n    checkReloadDisk();\n    int editorpos = _hlEditor.getSelectionStart();\n    _hlEditor.setText(_document.getContent());\n    editorpos = editorpos > _hlEditor.length() ? _hlEditor.length() - 1 : editorpos;\n    _hlEditor.setSelection(editorpos < 0 ? 0 : editorpos);\n}\n```\n\nNow I'm applying the edit to fix the cursor position.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"fd177b19-b89d-46f0-ae2b-e6bcd5d6249b","session_id":"ac3c3c7e-3944-4bdf-8f73-f3460c81d597","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"fd177b19-b89d-46f0-ae2b-e6bcd5d6249b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI now have a clear understanding of the bug. The issue is in `DocumentEditFragment.onResume()`:\n\n- When the user switches away from the app and back, `onResume()` is called\n- It calls `_hlEditor.setText(_document.getContent())` which **replaces the entire text**\n- `setText()` resets the cursor to position 0 (the beginning)\n- The cursor position is **never restored** after `setText()`\n\nHowever, in `loadDocumentIntoUi()` (lines 135-138), the cursor position IS properly preserved. The fix is to apply the same pattern in `onResume()`.\n\nLet me check the exploration agent's findings while I apply the fix:\n\n"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
